+# Task: attached `config.set` and the daemon's `/status` queued count (W50-a, D-16.549) Phase: follow-ups Owner: builder w50a
+
+## Status
+
+Done (2026-10-23). The daemon serves `config.set` (D-16.549 closed for the attached TUI): `/yolo`,
+`/reasoning`, `/fast`, `/verbose`, `/busy`, Shift+Tab and the model picker work attached; the
+server commands `/yolo`, `/reasoning`, `/fast` run on the daemon; the daemon's `/status` counts
+queued inputs. Outside the task's files: the dual-host allow-list (`bridge.settings` entry
+removed, stale) and `docs/notes/P17/dual-host-matrix.md`. Handed to the integrator: the ledger
+text of D-16.549 (closed) and D-16.1094 (only `/queue` and quick `exec` refused), RS30 / RS33
+wording, `docs/notes/P17/ws-endpoint.md` (still says `config.set` is unserved), D-ids for
+W50-a-1..7.
+
+Read: no reference file (our own attach path: the in-process bridge's `config.set` is the spec).
+Our `tui_bridge/methods_config.py` (`set_value`, `_set_session`), `tui_bridge/methods_slash.py`
+(`_yolo`, `_reasoning`, `_fast`), `service/client_settings.py`, `service/daemon_slash.py`,
+`service/slash_commands.py` (`_status`, `SlashHost.queued`), `service/daemon_host.py`
+(`_auto_approve`, `announce_info`), `service/session_mutations.py` (`model`), `service/subscriptions.py`,
+`gateway/ws/methods.py`, `state/runtime_ledger.py` (`pending`), the TUI's `slash/localCommands.ts`,
+`input/routeKeys.ts`, `pickers/modelPickerState.ts`, `docs/notes/P17/ws-endpoint.md` (W48-b, W48-h),
+`docs/notes/P17/dual-host-matrix.md`, the dual-host allow-list.
+Evidence: none.
+
+What it does (own words): a TUI attached to the daemon (the default) runs its `/yolo`, `/reasoning`,
+`/fast`, `/verbose`, `/busy` commands, Shift+Tab and the model picker by calling `config.set`. The
+daemon answered `-32601`, so none of them worked attached. Now the daemon serves `config.set` with
+the bridge's rules: the same keys, the same validation and error codes, the same scope (profile
+keys saved to the profile, session keys need a session this connection attached), the same result
+shape. The shared slash commands `/yolo`, `/reasoning`, `/fast` run on the daemon too (they were
+refused until `config.set` came, W48-h-2), and the daemon's `/status` counts the session's queued
+inputs (its durable queue), where it always said nothing.
+
+Inputs → outputs: `config.set {key, value, session_id?, confirm?}` over the daemon's WebSocket →
+`ConfigSetResult {key, value, applied, saved}` or an error (`INVALID_PARAMS`, `SESSION_NOT_FOUND`,
+`CONFIRM_REQUIRED`, `PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE`); a session switch that applied puts a fresh
+`session.info` into the session's events (every viewer's status bar). `slash.exec /status` →
+a `Queued messages: N` line while inputs wait.
+
+Files: `service/config_writes.py` (new: the shared validation and writes), `tui_bridge/methods_config.py`
+(delegates), `service/daemon_config.py` (new: the daemon's `config.set`), `gateway/ws/methods.py`,
+`service/subscriptions.py` (a connection's own tool-progress modes), `service/daemon_host.py`
+(`set_auto_approve`, `queued_inputs`), `service/slash_commands.py` (`/yolo`, `/reasoning`, `/fast`
+shared; `queued` async), `service/daemon_slash.py`, `tui_bridge/methods_slash.py`,
+`service/picker_reads.py` (`DAEMON_REFUSED` keeps `/queue` only), tests, the allow-list,
+`dual-host-matrix.md`, `ws-endpoint.md`, the ledger text of D-16.549 / D-16.1094.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes:
+- a session key without `session_id` → `INVALID_PARAMS` (path `session_id`), as the bridge;
+- a session this connection did not attach (another connection's) → `SESSION_NOT_FOUND`;
+- bad values (`busy=fast`, `yolo="yes"`, `fast=warp`, empty reasoning / model) → `INVALID_PARAMS`
+  with the bridge's message;
+- `/yolo` while an unattended (`-z`) turn holds the session's auto-approve: the person's choice wins
+  and the turn's end does not switch it back off (the host forgets its own switch);
+- a model switch while a turn runs → `deferred` (the session's mutation, applied at the next turn);
+  a model in `tui.confirm_models` or one whose window cannot hold the context → `CONFIRM_REQUIRED`
+  until `confirm: true`;
+- `/status` reads the queued count off the loop (a store read), 0 when nothing waits.
+
+Our design differences / decisions:
+- one module for the writes (`service.config_writes`) so both transports validate alike; the bridge
+  keeps its per-view parts (pending model, its own tool-progress mode, its projector);
+- the daemon's model switch goes through `session.mutate`'s `model` operation (the session's gate,
+  its row, deferred at the turn boundary), not a direct binding change;
+- `verbose` with a session is this connection's own mode for it (the bridge's mode is one viewer's
+  too); not saved, read back by `config.get` on the same connection. The daemon still sends every
+  tool event (no per-viewer projection yet): follow-up.
+
+Tests we will write:
+- contract over a real WS endpoint: each key attached equals the bridge's answer (busy, theme,
+  verbose with and without a session, yolo, fast, reasoning, model now / deferred / confirm), the
+  validation errors, session rules (none named, another connection's), `session.info` after a switch;
+- `/yolo`, `/reasoning`, `/fast` through `slash.exec` on the daemon, catalogue no longer
+  `unavailable` for them; `/status` with queued inputs;
+- unit: `config_writes` validation; the host's `set_auto_approve` beats an unattended turn's switch;
+- dual-host matrix: `bridge.settings` agrees, its allow-list entry removed.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- W50-a-1: one module for `config.set`'s checks and profile writes (`service.config_writes`); the
+  bridge's `methods_config` delegates to it (no change there: its contract tests pass untouched)
+  and keeps what is per view (the pending model, its viewer's tool-progress mode, its projector).
+- W50-a-2: `verbose` with a session on the daemon is this connection's own mode for that session
+  (`Subscriptions.set_tool_mode`), read back by `config.get` on the same connection, dropped when
+  it lets the session go; not saved. `session.info.tool_progress` stays the profile's (W48-h-6).
+  The daemon does not yet hide or trim tool events by that mode (the bridge's `off` / `new`
+  filter and argument / result caps): follow-up (a per-viewer projection in `Subscriptions`).
+- W50-a-3: the daemon's model switch over `config.set` is `session.mutate`'s `model` operation: a
+  deferred pick applies when the next turn starts (`before_turn`), where the bridge applies it as
+  soon as the running turn ends; the mutation's context-window check also answers
+  `CONFIRM_REQUIRED` (with its message) besides `tui.confirm_models`; a refusal answers
+  `PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE` with the mutation's message.
+- W50-a-4: `yolo`, `fast`, `reasoning` change the shared session for every viewer; each applied
+  switch puts a `session.info` into the session's events (all its viewers), as the bridge sends
+  its one viewer. `reasoning` is applied under the session's mutation gate.
+- W50-a-5: a person's `/yolo` while an unattended (`-z`) turn holds the run-scoped auto-approve
+  wins: the host forgets its own switch for that session, so the turn's end no longer turns it
+  off (`DaemonSessionHost.set_auto_approve`). The row is written off the loop before the switch;
+  a session with no row yet (before its first reply, D-16.426) keeps the switch live only, as in
+  `--local`.
+- W50-a-6: `/yolo`, `/reasoning`, `/fast` are shared server commands now
+  (`slash_commands.HANDLERS`, through the new `SlashHost.set_switch`); `DAEMON_REFUSED` keeps
+  `/queue` only and the daemon's catalogue lists the three as `server`. `SlashHost.queued` is
+  async; the daemon's `/status` counts the inputs waiting in the session's durable queue (every
+  viewer's, the running one excluded), where the bridge counts its viewer's own queue.
+- W50-a-7: no protocol change was needed: `config.set` was already declared (catalogue, generated
+  TS types, field docs); `codegen --check` and both twins' `--check` unchanged. Slice [b]'s
+  protocol additions do not meet this slice.
